        <mxCell id="p6s" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#5A6A80;" value="Map, scope, observe, record: in that order" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="14" width="356" x="822" y="306" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6div" parent="1" style="line;strokeColor=#C8E6C9;fillColor=none;strokeWidth=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="4" width="368" x="816" y="324" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6b" parent="1" style="text;html=0;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#2E7D32;spacingLeft=4;spacingTop=4;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="1. Map the session surface per role before any deployment &#xa;&#xa;2. Scope agent access below the natural session surface (dedicated profiles, structural not filtered) &#xa;&#xa;3. Session-layer visibility as a baseline, not post-incident &#xa;&#xa;4. Agent access recorded as a distinct identity event  Scope first, then observe. Not the other way around." vertex="1">
